DTEND:20260710T233000Z
SUMMARY:School of Melee (1st & 3rd NB Fighting Game Fridays)
DESCRIPTION:Noisebridge Hackerspace **School of Melee - SSBM Workshop & Tournament: Singles Competition & Self Improvement Mentorship** **Featuring Guest Speaker: LanTurN** **VOD Reviews and Mid-Set Coaching available to all (Bring your own USB with gameplay file)** School of Melee is a Melee focused workshop. The event will begin with a planned presentation\, followed by in person VOD reviews as well as mid set friendlies coaching. **Free Entry + Lossless Adapter Raffle** **Event Details** * Melee "TED-Talk" focusing on a variety of topics (tech skill\, match-ups\, etc.): 7:30 PM - 8:30 PM * Mid Set Friendlies Coaching provided by guest speaker * Melee Singles (32 player cap) * Singles: 8:30 PM - 11:30 PM ##### Location ##### NoiseBridge - 272 Capp St\, San Francisco\, CA 94110 **What is Noisebridge?** We are an accessible\, community-operated\, non-profit hackerspace for artists and audiences interested in the intersection of art\, technology\, and creative expression. We are a place to learn\, play\, create\, and share. Our facilities seek to provide infrastructure for work utilizing textiles\, music\, wood\, metal\, computer programming\, electronics\, science\, robotics\, space for performance or display\, and collaboration. You don't have to be a member or pay anything to participate in Noisebridge\, we're free and open. You just have to follow the one rule: Be Excellent to Each Other! **NOISEBRIDGE WEB SITE:** [http://www.noisebridge.net/](http://www.noisebridge.net/) **EVENT WIKI PAGE:** https://www.noisebridge.net/wiki/School_of_Melee **Getting Here:** Noisebridge is close to the 16th & Mission BART station\, and the 14 Mission\, 33 Stanyan\, and 49 Van Ness-Mission Muni buses. The 22 Fillmore and 12 Folsom Muni buses are within a couple blocks. ##### Parking: There are paid parking lots within walking distance\, or if you're lucky you can find street parking. **Hosts:** Angelo ([angelolyonsmedia@gmail.com](mailto:angelolyonsmedia@gmail.com)) **Discord:** Noisebridge Discord #School-of-Melee ##### Policies: Be excellent to each other is the guiding principle of Noisebridge. Wikipedia uses a somewhat similar rule\, which they call "the fundamental rule of all social spaces. Every other policy for getting along is a special case of it." Unlike Wikipedia\, Noisebridge takes a positive approach\, and avoids the practice of officially enumerating the myriad potential special cases\; "be excellent" is enough. ###### Limited spare controllers are available at request ###### Controller experts wanted for controller repair workshop | Source: DC415 San Francisco | Tags: security | https://www.meetup.com/noisebridge/events/315349959/
LOCATION:
URL:https://www.meetup.com/noisebridge/events/315349959/
END:VEVENT
